Suppose $A$ is positive definite, $B$ is symmetric, and
\begin{equation}
 \operatorname{rank}(B-tA)\ge2\quad\text{for every }t\in\R.
\end{equation}
For every real $h\ne0$, there is $U\in\operatorname{GL}_4(\C)$ such that
\begin{equation}
 U F_h(X)=-\tfrac18 G\Cr(UX)\qquad(X\in\C^4).
\end{equation}
Consequently $[F_h]$ is projectively conjugate to $[G\Cr]$.
In particular the positive-definite case of Remark 7.7 with simple generalized
spectrum is of type (A)-(i).
